A||N||9||fropuff||Anyone use Night Shades??||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||08-15-2000||11:20 PM||||Hey, I am soon doing DXR_DAD's back-up light mod on my '86 GT.  As soon as I get it buffed (tomorrow or Thursday.)  But, I was wondering if anyone has any experience using Night Shades.  It is a tinting spray that you can spray on light lenses to tint them.  I am going to spray them on the inside of the lens cover, since the bright glass doesn't match my tinted tail lamps.  Has anyone ever used this?  Also, I found this stuff at Mid America Designs; can I get it at an auto parts store or otherwise?  Thanks a lot.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||08-15-2000||11:39 PM||||I used that stuff on a 71 Buick (Taillights)I had. Its not bad, Just make sure what your painting is clean and try to do it in a dust free area. Apply several thin coats (them dry) untill its the shade your looking for.<P>Good Luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Dont forget to post some pic's<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||14
Z||000002||fropuff||08-16-2000||01:59 PM||||HAZE, Where did you find your Night Shades?  Would I be able to get it from an auto parts store?  THANKS. <P>Oh, I won't forget to post pics either!  Just gotta get it buffed, get my moldings back on, and get my back-ups in!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||08-16-2000||02:19 PM||||I got mine at a "Super Shop's" speed shop (Now Closed) But you should be able to get it at AutoZone or Pep-Boys <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||14
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||08-16-2000||11:01 PM||||At one time when I first thought of doing some kind of tail light mod I looked all over for that stuff(Night Shades) could not find it anywere!!!! I wanted that blacked out look<P>Good luck Puff I hope it turns out good<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000005||olympic||08-16-2000||11:08 PM||||  I remember seeing spray on(and stick-on) window tint that would produce a chrome or gold tint and looked like those reflective lenses on sungalsses.  I always thought it would be sweet to buy some clear headlight/taillight covers and coat them with this chrome tint.  Sort of "shades" for your car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||08-17-2000||12:26 AM||||how about doing the Night Shades treatment on the side marker lights also. All black body trim until the lights are on. Hmmm I might just have to give that a try. . .<P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||08-18-2000||02:48 PM||||Great idea, Cooter.  I decided that instead of getting some permanent tinting spray, I'm going to get a stick-on tint from Wal Mart.  I will stick it on the OUTSIDE of the lenses.  I am going to do the back-up lights, as well as the side markers.  (Thanks, Cooter.)  That way, I can remove it and re-apply if I screw up.  The tinting spray stays on FOREVER!  Thanks for the ideas.  ||||reg||10
Z||000008||GT Bastard||08-18-2000||04:13 PM||||I've used it... I ordered it from Summit Racing and put it on my old '85 IROC...  I thought is was pretty decent, but spray it on the INSIDE of the lens. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Terrybogin||08-18-2000||05:50 PM||||I used the stuff on my old 73 Camaro and followed the directons- spray the inside of the lenses- it did not make sense and you had to spray it so thick that you could not see the brake lights. On another set, I sprayed the outside very lightly and it worked great. I guess you should try it first on someting you would not mind wasting because they might be too dark.||||reg||1
